# IMPL-APP_DISPLAY_RESOLVER essence pseudocode

<!-- [IMPL-APP_DISPLAY_RESOLVER] [ARCH-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] [REQ-MACOS_PERM_REPORT] — human-readable app names from TCC client identifiers -->

## RESOLVE_BUNDLE_ID

```
INPUT: bundleId (client_type 0)
OUTPUT: displayName string
PRE: bundleId matches /^[a-zA-Z0-9.-]+$/
POST: returns CFBundleDisplayName or CFBundleName from app Info.plist when found
EFFECTS: scans /Applications and ~/Applications for matching CFBundleIdentifier; caches results
FAILURE_MODES: bundle not found -> FALLBACK_BASENAME(bundleId last segment)
```

## RESOLVE_PATH_CLIENT

```
INPUT: absolutePath (client_type 1)
OUTPUT: displayName string
POST: returns basename of path without .app suffix when applicable
```

## FALLBACK_BASENAME

```
INPUT: client string
OUTPUT: last path segment or substring after final dot for bundle IDs
```
